ö the initial coordinates of the dot, the distance d and the number of vectors. It is guaranteed that the initial dot is at the distance less than d from the origin of the coordinates. The following n lines each contain two non-negative numbers x i and y i ( 0ΓÇëΓëñΓÇë x i ,ΓÇë y i ΓÇëΓëñΓÇë200 ) ΓÇö the coordinates of the i-th vector. It is guaranteed that all the vectors are nonzero and different.\n\n## Output\n\nYou should print \" Anton \", if the winner is Anton in case of both players play the game optimally, and \" Dasha \" otherwise.\n\n## Examples\n\nExample 1:\n```\n0 0 2 3\n1 1\n1 2\n```\n```\nAnton\n```\n\n## Note\n\nIn the first test, Anton goes to the vector (1;2), and Dasha loses. In the second test Dasha with her first move shifts the dot so that its coordinates are (2;3), and Anton loses, as he has the only possible move ΓÇö to reflect relatively to the line y ΓÇë=ΓÇë x . Dasha will respond to it with the same move and return the dot in position (2;3).","type":"text"}],"contestId":69,"index":"D","memoryLimit":"256 megabytes","name":"Dot","problemKey":"69-D","rating":null,"tags":[],"timeLimit":"3 seconds","url":"https://codeforces.com/contest/69/problem/D"},{"approaches":[{"label":"Approach 1","number":1,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 2","number":2,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 3","number":3,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 4","number":4,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 5","number":5,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 6","number":6,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 7","number":7,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 8","number":8,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{